/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
**Description:**

Counts distinct elements in an array using a brute force approach. For each element, it looks back at all previous elements to check if it has already appeared. If not seen before, it increments the result counter. Time complexity is O(n²) and space complexity is O(1).

---

**Test Cases:**
```
arr = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}        => 5   // all unique
arr = {1, 1, 1, 1, 1}        => 1   // all same
arr = {1, 2, 1, 3, 2}        => 3   // mixed duplicates
arr = {5}                    => 1   // single element
arr = {}                     => 0   // empty array
arr = {-1, -2, -1, 3}        => 3   // negative numbers
arr = {0, 0, 1, 2, 0}        => 3   // zeros as duplicates
